From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Complete ADC sensor and peripheral probe lifecycles

Describe the internal PMK8350 die sensor instead of an empty ADC instance.
Bound eUSB2 wake NACK retries and never print an uninitialised revision.
Preserve PHY/OTG behaviour on an optional revision-query failure. Sort the
merged RX register defaults, use the current default workqueue API, and
classify deferred DSI and explicit SoundWire port overrides as probe state.
No display clocks, audio calibration gates or USB roles are removed.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
index 1d882db1d..8293b42e3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pmk8350.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/qcom,pmic-gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
@@ -1252,6 +1253,17 @@ eusb2_reset_default: eusb2-reset-state {
 	};
 };
 
+&pmk8350_vadc {
+	/* The PMIC's internal sensor needs no external board wiring. Battery
+	 * and USB measurements continue to come from PMIC GLINK.
+	 */
+	channel@3 {
+		reg = <PMK8350_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
+		label = "pmk8350_die_temp";
+		qcom,pre-scaling = <1 1>;
+	};
+};
+
 &pmk8350_rtc {
 	/*
 	 * Disabled upstream because not every SM8450-family board wires the RTC
